<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
  <head>
    <meta http-equiv="Content-Type" content="text/html; charset=utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
    <meta name="color-scheme" content="light">
    <meta name="supported-color-schemes" content="light">
    <title><%= site_name %></title>
  </head>

  <%# Light only: the two metas ask a client in dark mode not to invert the
      mail, and there is no dark rule. The layout's colours are named, not
      hex (whitesmoke, white, black, dimgray): a mail has no tokens. The
      violet is the button's alone (mails/_button), the one literal the
      design rules admit in a mail, and it is --cs-accent's light value
      (admin_design_rules_test). One column of at most 560px, system fonts,
      inline styles (a mail client reads no stylesheet), the site's name as
      text and no image: nothing is fetched when the mail is opened, so
      nothing can track it. %>
  <body style="margin:0;padding:24px 16px;background:whitesmoke;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.5;color:black;">
    <div style="max-width:560px;margin:0 auto;background:white;padding:32px;">
      <p style="margin:0 0 24px;font-size:20px;font-weight:700;"><%= site_name %></p>
      <%= yield %>
      <p style="margin:32px 0 0;font-size:13px;color:dimgray;"><%= t("mail.footer", site: site_name) %></p>
    </div>
  </body>
</html>
